The fix for this vulnerability is to sanitize the input and restrict it to only the intended directory. You can achieve this by checking if the provided file name is within the expected directory before reading the file. Here's an example of how to fix it:

```python
name = request.args["f"]
if name.startswith("/var/www/files/"):
    return open(name).read()
else:
    return "Invalid file name"
```

This code will only open and read files that are within the "/var/www/files/" directory, preventing file inclusion attacks.

